course: dictionary
lesson: 11293
title: Roman numerals: XIV
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Roman numerals are letters that stand for numbers. The main ones are I = 1, V = 5 and X = 10. XIV is made of X (10) and IV (4), so XIV means 14.
explain: When a smaller letter comes before a bigger one, you take it away: IV is 5 take away 1, which is 4. When a smaller letter comes after a bigger one, you add it: XIV is 10 plus 4.
explain: Kings and chapters use Roman numerals in their names. «Louis XIV ruled France from 1643 to 1715» means Louis the Fourteenth. Read XIV as a number, not as a jumble of letters.
fact: XIV is the Roman numeral for 14.
fact: X means 10 and IV means 4, so XIV = 10 + 4.
fact: Louis XIV means Louis the Fourteenth, a king of France.
fact: «Louis XIV of France ruled even longer, 72 years.» That is 1715 minus 1643.
fact: Roman numerals are also used in chapter numbers and on some clocks and buildings.
exercise: What is XIV in our numbers? | 4 | 104 | 41 | *14
exercise: In «Louis XIV ruled France from 1643 to 1715», what does XIV mean? | Fourteen letters | Four | *The fourteenth, as in Louis the Fourteenth | Fifteen
exercise: In the Roman numeral IV, what is the value of IV? | 6 | *4 | 3 | 14
test: Which number is XIII? | *13 | 3 | 11 | 31
test: Which Roman numeral means 9? | VI | XI | IV | *IX
exam: If Louis XIV ruled France from 1643 to 1715, how many years did he rule? | *72 | 27 | 62 | 82
